  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance for Banking &amp; Financial Services - Liberia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to assist the GoL in developing and maintaining a fair, safe, and stable financial sector that benefits and protects financial sector participants while maintaining public confidence in the financial system and supporting private sector-led economic growth. Project components will focus on: (1) strengthening the capacity of CBL banking and non-banking financial institution supervision to adequately regulate and supervise the banking and NBFI sectors; (2) establishing a deposit insurance regime that protects depositors in the event of bank failures and maintains public confidence in the financial sector; (3) developing and implementing an effective resolution framework that allows for the orderly resolution of failed financial institutions; (4) enhancing the CBL&apos;s capacity to monitor and react to macroprudential risks to financial sector stability; (5) strengthening the capacity of CBL insurance supervision staff to adequately regulate and supervise the insurance sector; and (6) enhancing financial sector compliance with International Financial Reporting Standards.</narrative>
  </description>
